WEBVTT

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.260
Er... I really am sorry about your 
poor treatment so soon after arri—

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:06.330
No matter.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.230
It was the result of my own carelessness.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:10.070
Huh?

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.500
Um...

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.020
But the others really were—

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.870
The initiation of hostilities was mutual.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.240
You really aren't mad?

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:20.490
Not at all!

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.830
He looks really mad!

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.750
I think that's how he looks all the time.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.010
I received your request to stay here with us.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.700
I heard you were a young... Saenome?

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.030
And that you were doing this 
to learn more about tsukumogami.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:41.340
The period is one year.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.230
Fortunately, we have rooms to spare,

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.950
and since the request came 
from a friend of Haori's,

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:47.980
as long as you respect 
the rules of the household,

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.360
you're free to make yourself at home.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.590
Do you have any questions for me?

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.410
<i>This girl, leader of a group 
of six tsukumogami...</i>

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.080
<i>Nagatsuki Botan.</i>

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:18.590
<i>Malevolent Spirits</i>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:37.010
<b>Shoreline</b>

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:43.820
<i>She doesn't look like she has enough grit 
to command a group of six tsukumogami.</i>

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.100
Shouldn't there be a sixth tsukumogami here?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.560
Nagi, you mean?

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.020
He's right here.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.560
Why... Why am I the only one tied up?!

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.120
What was that, Nagi?

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.070
It was Haori and the others who did it!

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:59.320
They beat him up when they stopped the fight!

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:03.030
The fight between Kunato-san... and <i>whom</i>?

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.350
Me.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.330
See?

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:06.890
You think about what you did.

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:09.330
Hold on! I've got work to—

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:10.730
Ahem.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:12.380
Any other questions?

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.590
<i>Perhaps she does have grit.</i>

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:16.820
Well, then...

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:23.690
Your manner of speaking suggests that, 
while you know of the existence of tsukumogami,

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:26.730
you are unfamiliar with the Saenome.

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:28.970
Yes, that is true.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:30.680
My apologies.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:34.400
The Saenome are humans 
empowered by Saenokami,

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.110
<b>Kunato</b>

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.920
the guardian god of the border between 
the lands of the living and the dead.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:42.610
<b>Kunato</b>

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:42.610
<b>Kunato</b>

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:42.230
We're like the police 
of the tsukumogami world.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:48.370
From that perspective, I'd like to give 
my opinion about your present situation.

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:51.540
It's untenable.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:57.380
Tsukumogami aren't like us. 
They're a breed of monster.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:01.220
Treating them like family 
is unthinkably dangerous.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:06.140
In practice, I've seen significant harm 
triggered from their association with humans.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.510
Their superior intelligence and power

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:11.020
lead them to view humans as disposable.

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:11.020
That son of a...

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:14.480
We're nothin' like those jerk tsukumogami!

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.770
Get a damn clue!

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:20.490
If it turns out they're toying 
with you in that same way,

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:21.780
I can't let it stand.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:25.100
Would you be willing to allow me 
to take over this case?

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:27.530
You can return to a normal life—

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:34.730
You don't know anything about my life.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:39.550
What gives you the right to say such 
presumptuous things? Such <i>insulting</i> things?!

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:42.750
I'm sorry, but I won't allow someone

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:46.430
who sees my family as monsters 
to remain in my home!

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.480
I'll admit that we treated you rudely as well,

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:52.560
so I'll allow you to stay for three days.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:58.330
But if, in that period, you show 
no intention of working together,

00:04:58.330 --> 00:04:59.860
I'll have to ask you to leave!

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:01.030
What?!

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:06.240
Don't forget! If you come back early, 
you'll be an ex-Saenome!

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.740
W-Wait!

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.520
How can we work together?

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:12.870
Ask the others!

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:20.500
Your room's at the end 
of the second floor hall.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:25.020
No comment.

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:27.470
You can't just make a girl cry, man.

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:29.560
Thbbt!

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:36.260
I saw no sign that she was being manipulated.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:39.580
<i>She meant what she said.</i>

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:42.710
<i>What did she mean by "working together"?</i>

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:46.490
<i>Cooperation?</i>

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:51.740
With that thing's brethren?

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.870
Someone got an earful!

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.760
Lucky you! You get a whole three days!

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:01.130
Show a little gratitude for Botan's kindness.

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:03.440
What do you want? To resume our fight?

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:07.480
Stupid. If we did that, 
you'd get kicked out on the spot!

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:11.900
Actually, I was thinking...

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:15.020
This might be a great chance 
to work together.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:16.520
What?

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:20.010
Mind hanging out with me for a while, kid?

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.480
You seem disheartened.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:25.900
I am.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:31.070
I know I got upset, but that deadline 
might have been a little too harsh.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:33.660
It's fine! Your anger was entirely justified.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:39.000
Hyoma-san's straightforwardness 
makes his issues very transparent.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:42.330
He's straightforward in 
the entirely wrong direction.

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:46.640
Why not just wait a while 
and see what happens?

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:47.820
Okay...

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.640
I'm going to have to see him at dinner!

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:58.940
<i>Kunato Hyoma... I hope to see soon...</i>

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:01.240
<i>whether you're worthy or not.</i>

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:02.900
Hold it.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:09.210
You want me to help you with your business... 
hunting down your own kind?

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:10.360
Yep.

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:13.700
I just got a request to seal 
a rogue tsukumogami.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.800
The conditions under which

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:19.880
the six tsukumogami are declared 
special exceptions and allowed to run free

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:25.320
are that they follow local 
Saenome requests for aid.

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:29.350
They are "Saenome Proxies" 
who hunt their own kind.

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:35.150
I'm not feeling 100% after
 being tied up like that.

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:36.650
Help me out a little,

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:40.820
and I'll tell Botan you acted like a decent guy.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:43.550
You want me to help you 
skip out on your work?!

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:46.110
Nah, it's "working together."

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:50.340
But either one's fine by me.

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:53.180
<i>Infuriating!</i>

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:57.140
<i>His irresponsible attitude makes it 
harder to accept his existence!</i>

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:02.040
<i>Why must I work with these creatures?</i>

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:08.100
You seem unconcerned 
about hunting your own kind.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:13.130
Is it your lack of a soul that makes 
it feel like a simple job to you?

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:14.780
Actually...

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:19.190
It makes other tsukumogami groups in 
the land of the living hate us and shun us.

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:22.270
It's a damned dirty business.

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:24.920
But all we wanted

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:27.610
was to be with her.

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.970
So that's what we do.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:34.530
You got anything like that in your life?

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:47.330
If not, what's it matter 
if you get sent back home?

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:50.010
Actually... I do.

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:53.530
That's why I can't afford 
to run away from this.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:56.460
So it's settled.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.970
<b>H
I
N
O
B
O
R
I
 
T
R
A
D
I
N
G</b>

00:08:57.520 --> 00:08:59.720
Which gang sent you, eh?!

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.100
How easy.

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:11.730
Were these also considered "weak"?

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:16.200
No... other humans are afraid of them.

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:18.970
They must be considered "strong."

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:19.910
Which means...

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:23.750
I am far superior to them!

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:27.370
Ah, he's already at it.

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:31.380
That awkward human form, 
that barely detectable presence...

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:34.620
Looks like a newborn tsukumogami to me.

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:37.130
Poor widdle guy!

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:41.810
Where's Hyoma-san?

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:44.190
Oh. Nagi dragged him out.

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:46.310
Nagi's helping him? Weird.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.810
That stuff Hyoma-san said...

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.570
It was presumptuous as hell,

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:55.580
but he said it out of 
genuine concern for Botan.

00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:58.280
I think Nagi picked up on that, just barely.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:02.030
You think we can all get along 
with Hyoma-san, then?

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.240
<b>Kunato</b>

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:17.260
<b>Kunato</b>

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:17.760
A hand towel, huh?

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:19.680
It's seen better days.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:22.300
That being his vessel explains a few things.

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:27.020
But nobody died, so let's count it as a win.

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:30.680
Don't worry. I'll put in 
a good word with Botan.

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:31.770
Huh?

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:34.020
You got hives from it?

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:36.990
I get it. You hate it that much?

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:38.280
Well...

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:43.760
<i>From working with tsukumogami... 
and helping them.</i>

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:53.100
A paper umbrella tsukumogami.

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:58.720
My brother and sister were killed 
by a paper umbrella tsukumogami

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.500
newly born into the land of the living.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.030
He's still alive.

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:08.580
But for some reason, I'm unable 
to access information about him.

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:12.190
No matter what trials 
I must endure to get there,

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:15.570
I must become the next head 
of the Saenome Kunato Clan.

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:18.820
If I do, I might be able to get a lead on him.

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:22.970
That's why, despite everything, 
I was willing to accept these conditions.

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:25.820
I'll try my best to get along, 
if that's what's required.

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:27.850
And...

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:31.960
I regret making Nagatsuki-san cry.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.690
You were really bothered by that, huh?

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:36.960
You think you could ever 
get along with Hyoma-san?

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:38.060
Probably not.

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:39.140
Definitely not.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.420
It's a job.

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:58.700
Excuse me! Breakfast is ready!

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:02.830
Regrettably, I haven't reached 
my training goals for the day.

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:06.410
You're more than welcome to eat without me.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:07.590
But...

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.960
I'll gratefully partake later.

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:13.020
He's uptight.

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.740
Um... would you like a refill—

00:12:17.740 --> 00:12:20.390
No. I'm imposing enough already.

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:23.340
<i>So uptight...</i>

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:30.270
<b>List of Kunato Hyoma supporters</b>

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:30.270
<b>-san</b>

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:30.270
<b>• Nagi</b>

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:26.520
You're using signatures?

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:30.270
Yes. We thought we should 
decide it among ourselves.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:34.830
He proposed this format himself, last night.

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:39.420
If he can earn the approval 
of all of us before the deadline,

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:41.540
he'll be allowed to stay.

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:43.620
Botan?

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:46.780
Hyoma-san's so uptight!

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:49.160
I hope it'll work out.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:52.300
He appears to offer 
100% in all his endeavors.

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:54.160
Yeah, I guess...

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:57.790
Apparently he's heading out on a job 
with Suzuri and Kagami today, and...

00:12:58.250 --> 00:12:59.850
I will see this through!

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:03.800
He could probably afford to relax a little.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:05.790
Maybe that's just his natural state.

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:07.390
Maybe...

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:09.360
Are you worried about something?!

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:10.360
About what?

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:12.470
Although...

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:14.490
Kagami should be fine,

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:18.980
but he and Suzuri might be a bad match...

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.980
I know <i>all</i> about the station area!

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:25.400
I'd be happy to show you my favorite shops!

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:27.770
Shady shops, huh?

00:13:27.770 --> 00:13:28.910
Of course not!

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:32.170
I'd never be courageous enough 
to enter one of those!

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:34.370
Anyway, you've got my email address!

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:36.520
Probably struck out there.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:38.630
Excuse me.

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:44.380
I just spotted a tsukumogami 
toying with humans.

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:45.440
Scary face!

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:47.380
D-Don't make it sound sordid!

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:51.440
I just want to make friends 
and talk about stuff!

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:53.520
I don't want anything more than a nice lunch!

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:55.890
I'm not doing anything shady, man! I mean it!

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:58.320
Why do you only approach women, then?

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:00.090
Personal preference.

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:02.320
Why don't you join me?

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.150
We could make it a double date!

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:06.900
We're supposed to be on a job, you dolt!

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.210
We've got time to kill first!

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:11.080
So where did the one called Kagami go?

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:12.410
She's...

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:16.100
I'm under threat!

00:14:17.030 --> 00:14:18.920
Every single one of you...

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:20.560
Chill out!

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:23.420
There's nothing wrong with 
getting some food on the road.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:24.800
I don't understand!

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:31.180
You join Nagatsuki-san 
for breakfast and dinner,

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:34.930
but tsukumogami have no need to 
engage in the practice of eating.

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:39.290
Why waste time and money 
to act as if you're human?

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:45.820
We just want to know what it's like... 
eating, picking out nice outfits...

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:49.450
Enjoying things the way that Botan... 
the way that people do.

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:53.950
Is that really... a waste?

00:14:56.550 --> 00:14:59.980
We care about things, you know.

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:05.800
I wish you'd try to see that 
without making negative assumptions.

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:12.420
Understood.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:16.920
I find the picking up of women 
personally inscrutable,

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:19.290
but the rest I comprehend.

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:22.600
And supplementing your nutrition 
before a job is fully acceptable.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:23.360
Huh?

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:25.940
I'll try my best.

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:29.360
All right, Hyoma-kun.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:33.120
We're about to meet a tsukumogami.

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:37.050
Try not to scare them 
with that death glare of yours.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:41.610
This request won't involve fighting.

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:45.080
It's the final "special exception" evaluation

00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:49.670
for a tsukumogami hoping to live 
alongside humans in this world.

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:50.590
<b>— Yagen —</b>

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:52.200
Hey there.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:55.350
I'm Suzuri, and I've been appointed 
your final evaluator.

00:15:56.420 --> 00:15:57.600
There's three of you?

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:00.080
The girl is my assistant, Kagami.

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:02.850
The man is a rookie Saenome.

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:09.110
She's a type of mortar wheel tsukumogami.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:11.600
She might be a little jumpy, 
I guess you'd say.

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:16.240
She's spent a long time terrified 
of being sealed away.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:18.110
We call it an evaluation,

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:20.220
but I know you've already 
received a job offer,

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:21.750
so it's more like final confirmation.

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:23.610
Really?

00:16:23.610 --> 00:16:25.760
I've heard rumors...

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:30.460
About tsukumogami who let their guard down, 
and get sealed away by force...

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:31.260
This isn't that.

00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:32.740
Don't worry.

00:16:33.350 --> 00:16:35.760
And I have a question for you.

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:38.810
Why did you choose to live on this side?

00:16:42.470 --> 00:16:45.770
I suppose... I feel safe here.

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:49.160
There's a nostalgic feel to this world.

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:52.030
I recognize that's a strange thing to say.

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:53.540
And yet...

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:59.910
Every now and then, we choose a vessel 
that's come to have a memory of its own.

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:02.950
The mortar wheel that became your vessel

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:06.010
might have felt at peace with its old life.

00:17:06.010 --> 00:17:09.590
That feeling of comfort transferred into you.

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:12.200
I see.

00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:14.670
That's a perfectly suitable reason to remain.

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:19.610
I completely understand how you feel.

00:17:19.610 --> 00:17:20.930
Don't worry.

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:23.630
Kagami.

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:24.730
Sure.

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:27.800
This is the tsukumogami, Kagami.

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:30.560
She's going to run the most 
crucial part of the process,

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:33.740
checking for a history of using 
your transformation powers for evil.

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:36.490
It's a just-in-case thing.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:38.990
<b>Property of Kyoto Saenome</b>

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:38.990
If you'd allow me...

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:41.490
Here we go.

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:05.110
That's the Shoyokyo—a mirror 
that reveals truth.

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:09.850
Right now, she's viewing everything 
there is to know about her.

00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:34.040
It all checks out.

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:35.550
She passes the evaluation!

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:36.920
Great!

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:38.550
Awesome work, everyone.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:41.720
Hyoma-kun,

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:45.130
I'm going to take her in to make the report.

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:47.160
You and Kagami can head back without me.

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:47.960
Right.

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:50.140
Call Botan, too.

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:52.570
Ask if she needs anything from the store.

00:18:52.570 --> 00:18:56.070
I'm afraid I don't have the number 
for the Nagatsuki household.

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:57.870
Oh, really?

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:00.240
Sorry, Kagami. I'll need you to ask—

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:01.820
Is there—

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:24.710
That was quite unexpected.

00:19:25.960 --> 00:19:28.220
I knew it. You tricked me!

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:30.940
You're the... the Nagatsuki...

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:38.810
You destroyed a Saenome Proxy 
and attacked his assistant.

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:41.610
Those are the facts as I see them.

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:43.660
You're the one who tricked us!

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:44.910
Hyoma-san!

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:47.660
I just want to stay here!

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:03.180
<b>Kunato</b>

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:04.050
Don't do it!

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:05.640
Hyoma-san!

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:06.350
<b>Kunato</b>

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:12.600
I... I've heard all about them.

00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:15.020
They hunt their own kind.

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:19.770
That's why... I...

00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:26.310
I see our infamy precedes us.

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:30.290
That's why the mention of the 
Nagatsuki name sent you into a panic.

00:20:32.110 --> 00:20:33.920
No need to worry.

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:36.790
We really did just come here to evaluate you.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.800
My special property kept you from killing me,

00:20:40.110 --> 00:20:42.680
and Hyoma-kun kept you 
from doing further harm.

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:44.970
All's well that ends well, I'd say.

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:49.810
Hyoma-san!

00:20:50.170 --> 00:20:53.520
She's got a pretty big shopping list for us.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:54.560
Right.

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:57.560
Kagami...

00:20:58.030 --> 00:20:59.900
What will happen to that tsukumogami?

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:01.870
She'll probably get her special exception.

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:05.700
She's a little paranoid, 
but they can work on that.

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:08.600
I personally hope she gets to stay, too.

00:21:09.010 --> 00:21:11.910
She loves the land of the living 
the same way I do.

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:15.830
Thank you.

00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:19.400
Suzuri told me to pass on the message

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:23.460
that you stopped when you 
saw the look in her eyes.

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:28.470
I said I'd try my best, 
and I didn't want to make myself a liar.

00:21:29.070 --> 00:21:30.220
That's the only reason.

00:21:38.300 --> 00:21:41.480
Keep it up, Hyoma-san!

00:21:41.880 --> 00:21:43.600
Kagami's not heavy enough.

00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:45.320
Let me in on that action.

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:46.320
Bring it on!

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:49.990
He's all right with being in contact 
with us if it helps with his training.

00:21:48.680 --> 00:21:49.590
Yes!

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:51.370
Hyoma-san!

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:53.240
The bath's warmed up. You should take one now.

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:59.640
Regrettably, I haven't reached 
my training goals for the day.

00:21:59.640 --> 00:22:01.750
I'll gratefully partake later.

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:04.630
He really is uptight.

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:12.760
<b>Messages Received</b>

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:12.760
<b>Kagami</b>

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:12.760
<b>Botan</b>

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:12.760
<b>I think Hyoma-san and I could
 get along after all!

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:10.380
<i>I think Hyoma-san and 
I could get along after all!</i>

00:22:10.380 --> 00:22:12.260
<i>I bet Suzuri feels the same way!</i>

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:13.850
Right!

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:18.270
<b>List of Kunato Hyoma supporters</b>

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:18.270
<b>-(san)</b>

